                <p class="mb-6">If you or someone you care about is dealing with severe obesity and related health problems, you may have already heard about bariatric surgery. But a very common question that most people have before making any decision is: <strong>what is done in bariatric surgery?</strong> Understanding exactly what happens during the procedure, why it works, and what changes it brings to your body can help you make a confident and well-informed choice about your health.</p>

                <p class="mb-6">Bariatric surgery, also known as weight loss surgery or metabolic surgery, is a group of surgical procedures that work by modifying the size or function of the digestive system to restrict food intake, reduce nutrient absorption, or both. These procedures are not cosmetic operations — they are medically proven interventions recommended for people with a body mass index (BMI) of 35 or above, or for those with a BMI of 30 or above who have serious weight-related conditions like type 2 diabetes or high blood pressure. If you are considering <a href="https://scodclinic.com/services/bariatric-surgery" class="text-scod hover:text-blue-700 font-semibold">Bariatric Surgery in Delhi</a>, it is important to understand what actually takes place inside the operating room and how it transforms your body long-term.</p>

                <p class="mb-6">In this complete 2026 guide, written in simple and easy-to-understand language, we will walk you through every aspect of bariatric surgery — from what happens on the operating table, to the types of procedures available, to what your body goes through after the operation. This blog is also reviewed under the guidance of <a href="https://scodclinic.com/about" class="text-scod hover:text-blue-700 font-semibold">Dr. Vijay Anand Reddy</a>, a highly experienced bariatric and metabolic surgeon, to ensure clinical accuracy and trustworthiness.</p>

